  "limits": [
    "This is the isolated diagnostic, not the complete production app playback/focus test.",
    "Native and JS use the exact same APK, page, six VIDs, complete-file download/decrypt and WebView playback path. The two engines run sequentially.",
    "Measurements include the whole Go process, not a separately isolated resolver heap. No forced GC was used.",
    "PSS snapshots depend on GC/scavenger and download timing; differences are not a fixed incremental runtime cost. The old V2 pair was 64561 vs 59680 KiB after six.",
    "peak_rss_kib is /proc VmHWM, a different measurement from current dumpsys PSS/RSS. RSS is not summed into unique physical memory.",
    "The native reference has its standalone ten-minute identity refresh cooldown; the JS prototype uses thirty seconds. Clean batches do not exercise that difference.",
    "Early cold empty responses are retained. Correcting a demonstrated registration encoding mismatch and passing subsequent batches does not prove that mismatch caused every empty response.",
    "SM3 is a standard generic host primitive; registration, signing/carrier math, timestamp/query construction, parsing and compatible-codec fallback remain JS.",
    "Node tests exercise this same source with async HTTP, but LG hardware and desktop runtime integration have not been accepted.",
    "Local-file activation uses a disposable signing key. Production online manifest/download/key/rollback integration is not completed.",
    "Goja provides cancellation and IO/stack limits, not a hard isolated JS heap quota. Only reviewed signed modules are suitable.",
    "Six short clips do not establish long-session stability or old-box performance."
  ],
